# Build output
dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Coverage
coverage.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html
*.coverprofile

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local-only notes (not committed)
*.local.md
*.local.*

# Guard only. The task list and its plans belong in a scratch directory,
# never here: they name the operator's machine, paths, and watched
# channels. This catches an export that lands in the repo by accident.
_tasks/

# Code review artifacts (local only)
.claude/review/

# Git worktrees for parallel development. The canonical checkout must not
# see their contents as untracked files.
.claude/worktrees/

# Working notes for whoever picks the build up next. They describe work in
# progress rather than the code, so they belong beside the checkout and not
# in its history.
.claude/handoff/

# Build settings. .env carries this machine's own values, and one of them is
# a Twitch application id tied to a single developer account. Its template is
# generated and committed, and holds no value at all.
.env
!.env.template

# Operator config. Running the quick start inside a checkout leaves a real
# config here, and a populated one names the watched channels and the
# library path. The config file can be called anything, so ignoring every
# .toml and re-admitting the checked-in template is the only rule that
# holds for a name nobody predicted.
*.toml
!config.default.toml

# Library state. .dvr holds library.db and the ownership marker; incoming
# holds the MPEG-TS a capture writes before it is remuxed and named.
.dvr/
incoming/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Recordings. These are capture.container's accepted values, and one file
# here is hours of a broadcast.
*.mkv
*.mp4
*.ts

# The sidecar written beside every recording, which carries everything the
# database holds about it: the channel, the broadcast title, the category,
# the timestamps and the library path. Ignoring the media and committing
# the record of it would publish the watched channels anyway, which is the
# same thing the *.toml rule above exists to prevent.
#
# Every JSON, then the four this repository does commit, because a sidecar
# is named after its recording and a name nobody predicted cannot be
# matched any other way.
*.json
!config.schema.json
!release-config.json
!.release-manifest.json
!.claude/settings.json

# A build with no -o lands here rather than in dist/, and the convention
# that says to use one is a convention rather than a rule.
/stream-dvr
/stream-dvr.exe

# Runtime logs, which carry channel names and library paths.
logs/
*.log
